Z||000000||Cooter||09-23-2000||09:18 PM||||I finally got the GT out and drove it across town to my dad's trade school so I could finish my hood scoop (pic's to come later). Some guy in a lowered Cherokee (yes, it was a Jeep!) with rice boy wire wheels pulled up beside me at the redlight. Before the light even changes green, he punches it! Then I guess he realized that the light was still red and stopped in the middle of the intersection. When the light finally goes green, he punches it again. Traffic was really bad, and his lane was pretty slow, so I just drove on by him. About 5 miles down the road, he comes flying by going at least 75 MPH in a 45 zone, cuts over in front of me and locks it down to make a right hand turn. I just dont understand the Ricer mentality- or lack of mentality!||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||09-23-2000||10:46 PM||||Sounds like you were headed through Anniston, cooter...Quintard Blvd. perhaps? I used to have the same prob 12/13 years ago in the Anniston/Jacksonville area (I went to h.s. in Jville) in my 84 Fiero, then in my 78 Trans Am...of course there werent ricers then, but you know, the more something changes, the more it stays the same!||||reg||1
